      "archaeologicalRemains": "substantive",
      "details": "<p>The gate\u2019s location is based on an aerial photograph of Nineveh taken in 1929, Corona satellite imagery (1967-68), and Google satellite imagery. The location of the gate suggested here is\u00a0the traditional spot of the\u00a0<span><a class=\"external-link\" href=\"../960751426\" target=\"_self\" title=\"Halzi Gate\">Halzi Gate</a>\u00a0</span><a class=\"external-link\" href=\"../960751425\" target=\"_self\" title=\"A\u0161\u0161ur Gate\"></a>according to most modern reconstructions of Nineveh. Those maps place the <span>\u0160ama\u0161 Gate</span>\u00a0about 1,600 m north of the southeast corner (approximate coordinates: <span>36.3506849, 43.1754063</span>), which is the proposed location of the <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"../960751428\" target=\"_self\" title=\"Mullissu Gate\">Mullissu Gate</a>.</p>",
      "review_state": "published",
      "accuracy_value": 5.0,
      "accuracy": "https://pleiades.stoa.org/features/metadata/google-earth-2016ff",
